{
  "name": "Email Management - Handle Long Random Waits",
  "id": "jaw9968-long-random-waits",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Assumptions (JAW-9968)\n- Schedule: every hour; `settings.timezone`: UTC; `executionTimeout`: 300.\n- Table `email_processing_waits` (`id`, `status`, `next_stage_at`, ...). Rows: `due` (schedule random delay) or `waiting` with `next_stage_at <= now()` (complete).\n- Random delay seconds: `$env.RANDOM_WAIT_MIN_SECONDS`–`$env.RANDOM_WAIT_MAX_SECONDS` (default 30–120); stored in `next_stage_at` (resume next run — no in-run Wait to avoid batch loop validator issues).\n- Up to 100 rows/run; dedupe on `id`. Logs: `email_wait_process_logs`, `workflow_error_logs`.\n- **Outreach Postgres**; Gmail → `$env.ADMIN_NOTIFY_EMAIL`. No PII in logs.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 540
      },
      "id": "9968aa11-bb22-4433-cc44-dd55ee667788",
      "name": "Assumptions",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
